  12/12 beat PNG

  THE A² PRINCIPLE IN ACTION:
  - CALIC uses gradient-of-gradient (second derivative = A² of pixel graph)
  - Error feedback uses context history (conditioning on A² profile)
  - Two-hop prediction uses neighbors of neighbors (literal A²)
  - Block classification uses curvature (second-order feature)
  ALL are manifestations of the same principle: A² captures more
  structure than A¹, at minimal extra cost (one more multiplication).

